nodecode-past is a rewrite of pastdotdev's pastdotdev/hermes-plugin:

  https://github.com/pastdotdev/hermes-plugin
  commit 22f7abdd1e73bebda6f876cd1f07fe383c25ada4
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 past (LICENSE)

The rewritten plugin is past_hermes of that commit. Its wire is carried over
unchanged: POST /api/v1/recall with a bearer project key, the query, the
identity, the limit and level "low", answering results with an occurredAt and
a content per memory; POST /api/v1/ingest/batch with items whose id is the
session's first sitting and then the session and the sitting's number, so a
resent sitting replaces its own. Its behaviour is carried over too: the
recall block with its marker, its count line and one dated line per memory on
a character budget; the same conservative redaction of keys and tokens on the
query and on the content; sessions cut into sittings where they went quiet,
at least five minutes, thirty unless the section says otherwise; content
hashes gating the send so an unchanged sitting is never sent twice; and the
cleaning of what Hermes or past injected from what the person said.

What changed: the harness seams are Nodecode's. The section of config.jsonc
is the config, recall rides the :round point and is written into the turn
with NLK:RECORD-TURN-CONTEXT-PROMPT instead of a provider's prefetch, a
finished turn arrives on the :frame point instead of through sync_turn, the
flush is a worker instead of a session-end callback, past_recall is a
registered tool and /past is a slash command instead of a provider's CLI.

What was left out, and why: the on-disk session buffer under ~/.past/hermes
and its crash recovery, because a cell keeps the running session in memory
and sends a sitting when it closes or when the cell stops; the shared
~/.past/config.json and the hermes pastdotdev setup / status commands, since
the section, /settings and /past are the same surface here and PAST_API_KEY
is still read; and the Hermes messaging-gateway opt-out, because a cell
cannot tell a shared room from a private session, so a home that serves
several people turns recall and ingest off or keeps a project per person.

LICENSE is past's repository LICENSE, unchanged.
